{"term":"stir","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:450f228a6e0464f836","definition":"To disturb the relative position of the particles (of a liquid or similar) by passing an object through it.","example":"She stirred the pudding with a spoon.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["agitate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:522f0388cd7f156da6","definition":"To disturb the content of (a container) by passing an object through it.","example":"Would you please stir this pot so that the chocolate doesn't burn?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fec0232d4bc4ea5b1d","definition":"To emotionally affect; to touch, to move.","example":"And what delights can equal those\n⁠That stir the spirit’s inner deeps,\n⁠When one that loves but knows not, reaps\nA truth from one that loves and knows?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8ba4c61ca713e0d0be","definition":"To incite to action.","example":"An Ate, stirring him to bloud and strife […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["arouse","instigate","prompt","excite","abet","actuate","goose","fuel","light a fire under","send","sting","bring about","cheer","draw","drive","encourage","egg on","engender","evoke","excite","foment","goad","grill","ignite","impel","incite","induce","inflame","instigate","invoke","lash","motive","motivate","move","obligate","oblige","push","promote","prompt","provoke","rouse","set off","spark off","spur","spur on","stimulate","stir","stir up","stoke","tempt","urge","whet","whip up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3dd1ffd52df999774a","definition":"To bring into debate; to agitate.","example":"Preserue the rights of thy place, but stirre not questions of Iurisdiction : and rather assume thy right in silence, and de facto, then voice it with claimes, and challenges.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3eea3e89ce2253ddc1","definition":"To disturb, to disrupt.","example":"They ſay he is the King of Perſea.\nBut if he dare attempt to ſtir your ſiege,\nTwere requiſite he ſhould be ten times more,\nFor all fleſh quakes at your magnificence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a5c23a51d3627c7b83","definition":"To change the place of in any manner; to move.","example":"[…] notwithstanding the swelling of my Foot, so that I had never yet in five days been able to stir it, but as it was lifted.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated, transitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:178a85c7afd4b90371","definition":"To begin to move, especially gently, from a still or unmoving position.","example":"And especially if they happen to have any superior character or possessions in this world, they fancy they have a right to talk freely upon everything that stirs or appears[…]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c4c6b9e3b02323f66","definition":"Of a feeling or emotion: to rise, begin to be felt.","example":"That night he was almost too happy to sleep, and so much love stirred in his little sawdust heart that it almost burst.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be7d149a07937c1cdc","definition":"To be in motion; to be active or bustling; to exert or busy oneself.","example":"All are not fit with them to stir and toil.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f9d67c75d5914d559","definition":"To rise from sleep or unconsciousness.","example":"“Mid-Lent, and the Enemy grins,” remarked Selwyn as he started for church with Nina and the children. Austin, knee-deep in a dozen Sunday supplements, refused to stir; poor little Eileen was now convalescent from grippe, but still unsteady on her legs; her maid had taken the grippe, and now moaned all day: “Mon dieu! Mon dieu! Che fais mourir!”","pos":"verb","synonyms":["arise","get up","rouse","abraid","arise","arouse","awake","awaken","get up","rise","rouse","stir","wake","wake up","waken"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be99c609358a572a06","definition":"The act or result of stirring (moving around the particles of a liquid etc.)","example":"Can you give the soup a little stir?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred","cause a stir","stirless","upstir"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b3ea236c924534b6a","definition":"agitation; tumult; bustle; noise or various movements.","example":"1668, John Denham, Of Prudence (poem).\nWhy all these words, this clamour, and this stir?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred","cause a stir","stirless","upstir"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e1b3b5ae8843bde7cf","definition":"Public disturbance or commotion; tumultuous disorder; seditious uproar.","example":"Being advertised of some stirs raised by his unnatural sons in England.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["astir","bestir","overstir","restir","stand and stir","stirabout","stirrable","stirrage","stirrer","understir","unstir","unstirred","cause a stir","stirless","upstir"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ca41480de